<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Asebu</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1874 CE (approx.) · capital Asebu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Fante coastal kingdom that invited the Dutch to the Gold Coast, sending envoys to the Netherlands in 1611.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Asebu was a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> kingdom on the coast east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast">Cape Coast</a>, with its port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moree">Moree</a>. It existed by the time Portuguese traders arrived in the late 15th century and resented Portuguese control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">gold trade</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elmina">Elmina</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Seeking new partners, Asebu's ruler sent envoys to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1611, and in 1612 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-nassau-gold-coast">Fort Nassau</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moree">Moree</a>, their first fort on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gold-coast-colony">Gold Coast</a>. Asebu then grew rich on gold and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>, while competing with neighbouring Fetu and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> states.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Asebu was absorbed into the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> group of states in the 18th century and joined the alliances against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>. It came under British rule with the creation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gold-coast-colony">Gold Coast Colony</a> in 1874 and remains a traditional area in Ghana.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1450 CE – 1874 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.56%;width:8.44%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1874 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Asebu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fante</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Asebu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1662&amp;focus=kingdom-of-asebu" aria-label="Kingdom of Asebu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4646 1983 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Asebu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4966 2239L4995 2226"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4995 2226h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4966 2239h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4966 2239h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Asebu. <a href="/atlas?year=1662&amp;focus=kingdom-of-asebu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

